==Latin==

===Etymology 1===
From Proto-Italic ''*gʷəgʷnai'', first person singular perfect active indicative of {{m|itc-pro|*gʷənjō|*gʷənisi}} ("to come"), from Proto-Indo-European {{m|ine-pro|*gʷegʷóme}} through the plural stem.

====Verb====
{{head|la|verb form|head=vēnī}}

# {{inflection of|la|veniō||1|s|perf|actv|indc}}

===Etymology 2===
From Proto-Italic ''*gʷənite'', second person plural present active infinitive of ''*gʷənisi''.

====Verb====
{{head|la|verb form|head=venī}}

# {{inflection of|la|veniō||2|s|pres|actv|impr}}

